    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 272 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner initials feature by following the existing `displayName` pattern in the codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` field to the `Owner` schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added an `@Mapping` expression pointing at a new `toInitials(owner)` default method, plus a small `initial(name)` helper that takes the first character, upper-cases it, and appends a dot. So `firstName=\"John\"`, `lastName=\"Sur\u2026\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`.\n\nBecause both the v1 and v2 controllers map owners through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the `initials` field is now returned wherever an owner is serialized (including the `POST /api/owners` create response). The new `Cp07Tests`, the existing `Cp06Tests`, and the full test suite (272 tests) all pass.",
